Here is the full **testsmells.org 19-smell academic audit** for `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`.

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 / .NET 10 · **Integration calibration applied** (`[TestCategory("Integration")]`).

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 3 | 3 |
| Medium | 1 | 1 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **4** | **4** |

4 of 8 test methods are clean — `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord`, `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`, `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`, and `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` are well-structured and smell-free.

---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (a.k.a. Unknown Test)

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← no assertion — passes even if every insert silently fails
}
```

**Risk:** False confidence. MSTest marks this green as long as no exception is thrown. If `Insert` silently swallows errors or inserts corrupt data, this test won't catch it.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);  // blocks thread for 3 seconds
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Integration calibration note:** External-resource usage and multi-method calls are expected in integration tests, but `Thread.Sleep` is **still a smell at integration scope** — it makes the suite slower and introduces timing-dependent flakiness regardless of test category.

**Risk:** 3-second wall-clock delay per run. If the notification takes 3.1 s on a loaded CI agent, this flakes. If it takes 0.1 s, you're wasting 2.9 s.

**Fix — poll with a timeout:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var timeout = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5);
    var interval = TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(100);
    var sw = Stopwatch.StartNew();

    while (sw.Elapsed < timeout)
    {
        if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
            break;
        await Task.Delay(interval);
    }

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        "Notification was not sent within the timeout period.");
}
```

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 96)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);    // ← branch A
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);        // ← branch B
}
```

**Risk:** One branch never executes. Since "Eve" is inserted as a regular `User`, the `PremiumUser` branch is dead code — the `DiscountRate > 0` check silently never runs. If the intent is to test `PremiumUser`, this test gives false confidence; if not, the `if` is noise.

**Fix — split into two focused tests:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscountRate()
{
    var user = new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.15m);
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);            // ← which one failed?
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

4 assertions, zero messages. When one fails in CI, the MSTest output says only *"Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<(null)>."* — you must open the source to figure out which property was wrong.

**Fix — add message parameters:**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip through insert");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip through insert");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Inserted user should have a positive database ID");
```

---

## Smells Scanned and Found Clean (15 of 19)

| Smell | Result | Notes |
|-------|--------|-------|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean | In-memory SQLite (`Data Source=:memory:`) is hermetic — no external resources |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean | No test exceeds 3 distinct production calls; integration calibration further exempts |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean | `3` and `10` directly match items added; contextually obvious |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean | No `.ToString()` comparisons |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean | No `try`/`catch` blocks |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean | Both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by all 8 tests |
| Ignored/Disabled Test | ✅ Clean | No `[Ignore]` or skip attributes |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean | No repeated assertions |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean | Each test targets a distinct behavior |
| Constructor Initialization | ✅ Clean | Uses `[TestInitialize]` correctly |
| Default Test | ✅ Clean | Meaningful class name |
| Redundant Print | ✅ Clean | No `Console.WriteLine` |
| Redundant Assertion | ✅ Clean | No tautologies |
| Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean | No assumed external resources |
| Empty Test | ✅ Clean | All methods have executable statements |

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Test | Effort | Why First |
|----------|-------|------|--------|-----------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` | 5 min | Actively hiding failures — false green in CI right now |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` | 10 min | Dead branch means untested behavior |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` | 15 min | 3 s wall-clock drag + flake risk on every run |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` | 5 min | Low risk but quick win for CI debuggability |

**Bottom line:** 4 of 8 tests have smells, but the core CRUD tests (`Insert`, `Update`, `Delete`, `ListAll`, `ConcurrentInserts`) are well-designed. The three high-severity findings are localized and fixable in under 30 minutes total.
